# Source files are text, always. A raw control byte in a source file makes git
# store it as a binary blob — no diff, no blame, no grep — which is how 197
# lines of production code once merged with a zero-line diff (M14 audit).
# `text` guarantees line-ending normalization and, more importantly, makes any
# file git still classifies as binary show up as a loud anomaly in review.
*.ts text
*.tsx text
*.rs text
*.md text
*.yml text
*.yaml text
*.json text
*.html text
*.css text
*.sh text eol=lf
*.toml text
